# Unit21
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit21核心词汇

consensus/kənˈsensəs/共识/The committee reached a consensus on the issue.
consent/kənˈsent/同意/You need parental consent for this activity.
conservative/kənˈsɜːrvətɪv/保守的/He holds conservative political views.
considerable/kənˈsɪdərəbl/相当大的/She has considerable experience.
consistent/kənˈsɪstənt/一致的/Her work has been consistently excellent.
constitute/ˈkɑːnstɪtuːt/构成/Women constitute 60% of the workforce.
contemplate/ˈkɑːntəmpleɪt/沉思/She contemplated the meaning of life.
contemporary/kənˈtempəreri/当代的/She is a contemporary artist.
contend/kənˈtend/竞争/He contended that the decision was unfair.
contradict/ˌkɑːntrəˈdɪkt/反驳/The evidence contradicts his testimony.
controversial/ˌkɑːntrəˈvɜːrʃl/有争议的/The topic is highly controversial.
convention/kənˈvenʃn/惯例/It is a convention to shake hands.
conventional/kənˈvenʃənl/传统的/She has a conventional approach.
cooperate/koʊˈɑːpəreɪt/合作/The two companies agreed to cooperate.
coordinate/koʊˈɔːrdɪneɪt/协调/We need to coordinate our efforts.
corporate/ˈkɔːrpərət/公司的/The company has a strong corporate culture.
correspond/ˌkɔːrəˈspɑːnd/对应/The results correspond with predictions.
corrupt/kəˈrʌpt/腐败的/The corrupt official was arrested.
counsel/ˈkaʊnsl/建议/She sought legal counsel.
counterpart/ˈkaʊntərpɑːrt/对应的人/He met with his counterpart.
crack/kræk/裂缝/There is a crack in the wall.
craft/kræft/工艺/She learned the craft of pottery making.
crash/kræʃ/碰撞/The stock market crashed in 2008.
creative/kriˈeɪtɪv/有创造力的/She is a creative designer.
criterion/kraɪˈtɪriən/标准/What is the criterion for selection?
criticism/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/批评/He faced harsh criticism.
crucial/ˈkruːʃl/关键的/This is a crucial decision.
cultivate/ˈkʌltɪveɪt/培养/We should cultivate good habits.
currency/ˈkɜːrənsi/货币/The exchange rate fluctuates daily.
curriculum/kəˈrɪkjələm/课程体系/The school revised its curriculum.
database/ˈdeɪtəbeɪs/数据库/The company maintains a large database.
deadline/ˈdedlaɪn/截止日期/Please submit the report before the deadline.
debate/dɪˈbeɪt/辩论/The students held a debate on education reform.
decade/ˈdekeɪd/十年/Great changes have taken place in the past decade.
decline/dɪˈklaɪn/下降/The number of students declined this year.
dedicate/ˈdedɪkeɪt/致力于/She dedicated her life to helping the poor.
deficit/ˈdefɪsɪt/赤字/The government is trying to reduce the deficit.
define/dɪˈfaɪn/定义/How do you define success?
deliberate/dɪˈlɪbərət/故意的/It was a deliberate attempt to mislead.
delicate/ˈdelɪkət/精致的/This is a delicate matter.
deliver/dɪˈlɪvər/递送/The company delivers goods nationwide.
demand/dɪˈmænd/要求/There is a growing demand for organic food.
democracy/dɪˈmɑːkrəsi/民主/Democracy is based on equality.
demonstrate/ˈdemənstreɪt/证明/The experiment demonstrates the theory.
deny/dɪˈnaɪ/否认/He denied all the charges.
depict/dɪˈpɪkt/描绘/The painting depicts a beautiful landscape.
depress/dɪˈpres/使沮丧/The downturn depressed spending.
deprive/dɪˈpraɪv/剥夺/War deprived children of education.
derive/dɪˈraɪv/来源于/The word is derived from Latin.
deserve/dɪˈzɜːrv/应得/She deserves recognition for her work.
